since `tier` could be null, in that case i believe we would return 10k but i think we want 100 instead

so i think we could do something like this to protect against that:

```
  const tier = authParams?.tier ?? "free";

  if (tier === "free") {
    return 100;
  }
```

otherwise lgtm thanks!

